From 7ba39243ce2f34ecd9a97168b536ce54526a7188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "JQE Chief Engineer (Claude)" <jqe-bot@example.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:28:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/37] fix: BacktestEngine.execute_trade's argument-count bugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

execute_trade(signal, candle) called approve_trade(signal) — missing
the required market_data argument — and simulate_trade(signal, candle)
— missing current_index; simulate_trade needs a full DataFrame plus a
position within it to search forward from, not a single candle. Both
would have raised TypeError on first real use; neither had ever
actually been exercised (see docs/architecture.md, Milestone 1's
original discovery).

Fixed signature: execute_trade(signal, current_index, dataframe).
Passes dataframe.iloc[:current_index + 1] to the risk engine (history
only, never the future) and the full dataframe + index to
simulate_trade (which enforces its own no-look-ahead guarantee).

Also adds type hints, docstrings, and records lot_size on each trade.

8 tests covering the no-trade/risk-rejected paths, win/loss balance
updates, and a regression test confirming the risk engine never sees
data past current_index.
